  "transcriptContext": "Vale’s original examples on our table, heads-up. As she names ace-seven-two, the three empty flop slots light one by one; that dry board is never dealt, and her words about it sit beside the table. As she says jack-ten-nine, the flop J♠ T♠ 9♥ deals. Vale names ranks only, so the suits are given for the example: two spades add the flush draw that makes a combo draw possible. Your ace-queen, the pot of 60 and the stacks of 970 (a raise to 30 on the button and a call from the big blind) are also given for the exercise; she does not speak them. As she says what the wet board creates, the words pairs, straights, two pairs and combo draws appear under the table, the flop cards lift, and the two spades light on combo draws. As she names the caller, Ace Andy checks to you. As she says to read the texture before you bet, her three questions appear beside the table, and none is answered. The film shows no bet, recommends no action, assumes no range and turns over no opponent card. The original voice and speaking animation play continuously at their original speed.",
